<TITLE>Ignition Coil with Igniter</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>By placing a coil independently for each cylinder, the distributor and high-tension cords are eliminated, reducing losses in the high-voltage section, ensuring reliability and reducing radio noise.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A compact, lightweight igniter is built in, and a high voltage is induced in the secondary (No. 2) coil by the signal from the engine control computer.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
